  "Description": {
    "Cost": 4046738,
    "UIName": "Hei Lian",
    "Id": "chassisdef_hei_lian_HEI-C3",
    "Name": "Hei Lian",
    "Details": "The original variant of the Hēi Lián was the C3, which carried a Boosted C3 Master. No one remembers anymore why the decision was made to combine a C3 with stealth equipment, but this is the result. Besides the C3 Master, the variant carries a Gauss Rifle and an ER PPC in each arm, supported by two Extended Range Large Lasers and two Medium Pulse Lasers in the right torso. Two Extended Range Medium Lasers in the head, wrap up the design.\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Quirk: Breaching Shot</color></b>\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Drop Cost Multiplier: 1.38</color></b>",
    "Icon": "uixTxrIcon_ironclad"
  },
  "VariantName": "HEI-C3",
  "ChassisTags": {
    "items": [
      "Superheavy",
      "mr-resize-1.12-1.15-1.02"
    ]
  },
  "StockRole": "Stealth Superheavy",
  "YangsThoughts": "When the RISC laboratories developed the superheavy version of the Wraith Suppression Shield System, they wanted to see how it fared in actual combat at a larger scale before they re-geared to their own heavily over-utilized superheavy factories. Three of the Great Houses were persuaded to design a number of superheavy 'Mechs around the system, all three ending up with very similar looks due to the prototype stealth system requirements and pre-designed components supplied by the Republic. The house Liao result was the Hēi Lián, translating to Black Lotus from mandarin, a 170 ton superheavy focused on delivering a powerful punch at enough range to have a chance to remain hidden after firing.",
